      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nint main() {\n\tint n,s;\n\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\n\tstd::vector<std::vector<int> > matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n\tfor(int i=0;i<n;i++)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<n;j++) \n\t\t\tscanf(\"%d\", &(matrix[i][j]));\n\n\tassert(s<n);\n\tassert(n<8000);\n\tassert(s>0);\n\tassert(n>0);\n\n\tint sum = 0;\n\tfor(int i=0;i<s;i++)\n\t\t#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum)\n\t\tfor(int j=0;j<s;j++)\n\t\t\tsum += matrix[i][j];\n\n\tint mxSum = sum;\n\n\tint dir = 1;\n\tint i = 0;\n\tint j = 0;\n\twhile(i+s <= n) {\n\t\tif( (j+s == n && dir==1) || (j==0 && dir==-1) ) { \n\t\t\tint exitingRow = i;\n\t\t\tint enteringRow = exitingRow+s;\n\t\t\tif(enteringRow >=n) break;\n\n\t\t\t#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) {\n\t\t\t\tsum += matrix[enteringRow][k+j] - matrix[exitingRow][k+j];\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\ti++;\n\t\t\tdir*=-1;\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tint exitingCol, enteringCol;\n\t\t\tif(dir==1) {\n\t\t\t\texitingCol = j;\n\t\t\t\tenteringCol = exitingCol + s;\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tenteringCol = j-1;\n\t\t\t\texitingCol = enteringCol + s;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t#pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum)\n\t\t\tfor(int k=0;k<s;k++) {\n\t\t\t\tsum += matrix[k+i][enteringCol] - matrix[k+i][exitingCol];\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tj+=dir;\n\t\t}\n\t\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum,sum);\n\t}\n\tprintf(\"%d\\n\",mxSum);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining the subtract-old and add-new loops in both row and column sliding-window updates into a single loop with an OpenMP SIMD reduction preserves all loop-carried dependencies (the window sum is still updated atomically per iteration) while reducing loop overhead and exposing one vectorizable reduction instead of two. The combined expression `sum += new - old` keeps the accumulator closer to its final value, which also reduces intermediate overflow risk.",
  "notes": "Only src/solution.cpp was modified. The snake traversal order is unchanged; each update still removes exactly one row/column and adds exactly one row/column before updating mxSum. SIMD pragmas are ignored if OpenMP is not enabled, preserving baseline behavior.",
